   "source": [
    "### Getters"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "e229e6c2-6da9-4df9-afad-9eebdfcc6e6b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Getters in Python are methods that are used to access the values of an object's properties. They are used to return the value of a specific property, and are typically defined using the @property decorator. Here is an example of a simple class with a getter method:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "92eafed6-d8b0-46d0-95ac-f2f34ac73e1f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Value is 10\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "class MyClass:\n",
    "    def __init__(self, value):\n",
    "        self._value = value\n",
    "\n",
    "    def show(self):\n",
    "        print(f\"Value is {self._value}\")\n",
    "    @property\n",
    "    def value(self):\n",
    "        return self._value\n",
    "\n",
    "obj = MyClass(10)\n",
    "obj.show()"
   ]
  },
